WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.901
Parts of Southern California

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.970
reeling from intense rainfall

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.306
caused by Tropical Storm Hillary.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.774
Palm Springs alone

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.976
saw nearly a full year's worth of rain

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.212
in just 24 hours.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.446
CNN's Stephanie

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.582
Elam is in the Cathedral City for us

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.385
in California, right near Palm Springs.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.620
What are you seeing, Stephanie?

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.390
Still seeing a lot of mud

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.058
out here in the earthmovers or out

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.493
trying to clean it up here.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.427
What else I can tell you?

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:27.994
We just learned

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.996
that Interstate Ten is open.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.064
However, there's a catch.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.931
You have to get off the freeway

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.732
and get back on it.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.034
Whether you're going east or west.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.669
And that's what that line of semi-trucks

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:37.871
is up there waiting for.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.639
But all in all, across

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.007
Southern California,

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.976
there is a lot to clean up after Hillary

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.114
Southern California

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.751
facing unprecedented flooding

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.954
holy violent mudslides,

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.056
flash floods,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.757
damaging roads and homes

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.425
after bearing

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.527
the brunt of Tropical Storm Hillary.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.761
There's a lot of destruction

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.596
in rivers of flash flood water

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.531
taking over the streets

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.299
of Cathedral City overnight

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.535
and neighborhoods in nearby Palm Springs.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.036
Into the early morning,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.204
piles of thick

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.273
mud left behind from floodwaters

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.542
blanketing everything in sight.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.843
The mud inescapable

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.845
for anyone attempting to get around.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.447
We're absolutely telling people

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.849
if they don't have to be out

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.484
to stay in their homes.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.019
One, the roads,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.121
we're still assessing the damage

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.123
and the places where there's still water

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.224
and mud over the roads.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.792
We don't know how safe those are.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.493
Jay Bubbler

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.028
spent the night into the morning

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.129
rescuing drivers

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.131
stuck on flooded and muddy roads.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.032
What kind of conditions

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.600
were you seeing while you were out there?

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.534
Cars floating

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.435
and there was cars

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.603
that were almost washed out.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.004
He echoed authorities warnings

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.406
to stay off the roads.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.640
A lot of them are regretting

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.109
that they tried to get across to it

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:49.476
to save it.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:49.809
Over here,

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.510
they have dad's car

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.744
and Dad doesn't know it yet.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.712
So I'm guessing around it.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.814
When you see water, you don't cross it.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.582
The area around

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.282
Palm Springs

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.418
saw nearly a year's worth of rain

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.520
in just 24 hours.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.688
I spent the night on the roof

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.489
of my truck,

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.158
disabling 911 emergency calls overnight.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.559
Downtown Los Angeles

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.727
experienced the rainiest

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.662
summer day on record, going back

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.231
more than 100 years.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.433
Los Angeles was tested,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.468
but we came through it.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.202
The Los Angeles

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:16.903
Fire Department

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.238
fielded more than 4000

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.973
emergency calls on Sunday.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.742
And responded to about 800 incidents.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:23.643
Los Angeles

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.512
Public Schools were closed on Monday,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.713
while officials surveyed

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.314
facilities for damage.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.383
Take all those conditions into account.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.385
After careful consideration,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.120
we decided to shut down the schools.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.488
Right decision.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.990
The Los Angeles Angels to play

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.925
the Cincinnati Reds on Wednesday,

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.293
postponing their home game

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.961
because of the effects from the storm

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.432
so much rain in San Diego.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:49.068
A tower of water was seen erupting

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.537
from a manhole today.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.771
The city saw its rainiest

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.707
summer day in over 170 years.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.376
Getting ten times

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.044
their average summer rainfall

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.612
in just one day.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.513
The cleanup effort

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.614
the top priority

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.582
after the rain

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.283
with Hillary

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.451
continuing to move through the west.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.353
Millions will still remain under flood

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.956
watches from California to Idaho.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.528
And back out here in Cathedral City.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.930
Wolf, you just got to see how thick

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.597
this mud is.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.464
Even after the water

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.866
has been receding through the day.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.801
I can still sink down into it.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.736
Here, and that is what's encased.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.005
These couple of cars here behind me.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.407
And I know that they got there now

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.842
by floating in the thick of the storm.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.243
That shows you

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.544
how fast the water was moving.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:31.945
Out there.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:32.478
In the distance,

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.413
you may hear more equipment

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:33.780
and that's

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.815
because they're digging out homes

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:36.449
in some of these

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.784
residential neighborhoods Wolf.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.519
Yeah, a terrible, terrible situation.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.420
Stephanie Elam,

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.521
thank you for that report.

